    "name": "Black Gravenstein Apples",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Black Gravenstein apples are a rare, heirloom variety featuring a uniquely dark, richly blushed red-and-green skin with crisp, juicy, and sharply tart-sweet flesh.</span></p><ul class=\"lexical-text-editor--list-ul\"><li value=\"1\"><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Taste and Texture</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">: Crisp and fine-grained flesh with a bold, tangy, sweet-tart flavor and a strong, sweet floral aroma.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Best Uses</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">: Exceptional for baking, making silky applesauce, pressing into cider, or slicing fresh for a tart snack.</span></li></ul>",
